---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for projectinsomnia.com.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p>
    Reading this site collects nothing about you. No analytics, no tracking,
    no cookies, no accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>The newsletter</h2>

  <p>
    If you sign up on the <a href="/subscribe/">subscribe page</a>, you're
    handing over information on purpose, so here's where it goes.
  </p>

  <p>
    The form runs on <a href="https://docs.netlify.com/manage/forms/submissions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Netlify Forms</a>.
    Netlify stores each signup: your email address, plus the IP address,
    browser user agent, and referring page that came with the request. The
    site then passes your email address and IP address
    to <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buttondown</a>,
    which sends you a confirmation email. Nothing gets sent until you click
    the link in it. After that, Buttondown emails you when a new post goes
    up. I use your address for that and nothing else. I don't sell it, and
    nobody gets it beyond those two services.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every newsletter has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing stops the
    emails, but it doesn't erase you: Buttondown keeps the record marked as
    unsubscribed, and Netlify still has the original signup. If you want
    those deleted too,
    email <a href="mailto:andrew@projectinsomnia.com">andrew@projectinsomnia.com</a> and
    I'll delete your signup from both. What each company keeps in its
    own logs and backups after that is covered by its own privacy policy,
    linked above.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>

  <p>
    If you email me, I have your email address and whatever you wrote. I use
    it to reply to you. That's it. I don't share it or sell it. If you want it
    deleted, email <a href="mailto:andrew@projectinsomnia.com">andrew@projectinsomnia.com</a> and
    I'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>

  <p>
    The site is hosted on <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Netlify</a>,
    which may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses) like any web
    host. A few pages load images from third-party services, which see those
    requests the same way.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
